dsh-companion README · Optional Billing Integration：The plugin does not depend on `dsh-billing`. When that plugin is installed in the current Web profile, Companion reads its public, read-only `billing` session projection and shows:

- turn and session cost;
- cumulative tokens and quota progress;
- the number of unpriced models.

dsh-companion README · Privacy Boundary：The Host projection stores only status, turn, tool name, timing, and an error code. It does not store or display:

- user prompts or model responses;
- tool arguments or tool results;
- API keys, request headers, or full provider error messages;
- workspace file contents or paths;
- external telemetry identifiers.
